---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { MAINTAINER, REPO_URL, withBase } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base title="About" description="What Med Tables is, who maintains it, and how to contribute.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <h2>What This Is</h2>
    <p>
      Med Tables is a free, open-source collection of reference tables for clinicians: dose conversions, equivalence
      tables, and checklists such as the H's and T's. Every table cites its sources and shows its caveats.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site has no ads, analytics, cookies, or trackers. It works on a phone, in dark mode, offline once visited, and
      on paper.
    </p>

    <h2>Who Maintains It</h2>
    <p>Med Tables is maintained by <a href={MAINTAINER.url}>{MAINTAINER.name}</a>.</p>

    <h2>How to Contribute</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues/new?template=new-table.yml`}>Propose a new table</a> using the issue form.</li>
      <li>Report an error with the link at the bottom of any table page.</li>
      <li>
        Edit or add a table directly with a pull request. See{' '}
        <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>CONTRIBUTING.md</a> for the data format, reference
        requirements, and review process.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Licenses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Code: <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>MIT License</a>.</li>
      <li>
        Table content: <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0</a> (CC BY
        4.0). You may share and adapt it with attribution.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>Please also read the <a href={withBase('disclaimer/')}>disclaimer</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
